@startuml GITGLE Search & Ranking Architecture
title GITGLE: Search Query Processing & TF-IDF Ranking Pipeline

participant User
participant Query as "Query\nProcessor"
participant Index as "Inverted\nIndex"
participant Scorer as "Scoring\nEngine"
participant Results as "Result\nFormatter"
participant Display as "CLI Display"

== QUERY PARSING ==
User -> Query: "python framework"
activate Query

Query -> Query: Tokenize\n["python", "framework"]
Query -> Query: Lowercase\n["python", "framework"]
Query -> Query: Stem\n["python", "framework"]

== INDEX LOOKUP ==
Query -> Index: Look up term: "python"
activate Index

Index -> Index: Find in inverted index:\ninv:full-index["python"]
Index -> Index: Return postings list:\n[{repo: google/gson,\nfreq: 29,\ntfIdfScore: 38.278},\n{repo: aio-libs/aiohttp,\nfreq: 0,\ntfIdfScore: 7.656}, ...]

Index -> Query: Return 6 matching repos
deactivate Index

Query -> Index: Look up term: "framework"
activate Index
Index -> Index: Find in inverted index:\ninv:full-index["framework"]
Index -> Index: Return postings for "framework"
Index -> Query: Return matching repos
deactivate Index

== RESULT MERGING ==
Query -> Query: Merge results from\nboth terms
Query -> Query: Union of matching repos

Query -> Scorer: Submit results for\nfinal ranking

== TF-IDF SCORING ==
activate Scorer

Scorer -> Scorer: For each repo:

note over Scorer
  **Score Calculation:**
  
  **Base TF-IDF:**
  score = TF × log(totalDocs / docFreq)
  
  For term "python":
  - TF (in django-rest-framework) = 5
  - docFreq = 6 repos have "python"
  - totalDocs = 114 repos
  
  score = 5 × log(114/6)
        = 5 × log(19)
        = 5 × 2.944
        = 14.719
  
  **Metadata Boost Factors:**
  - Language: Python → 1.3×
  - Stars: 29974 (>1000) → 2.0×
  
  **Final Score:**
  14.719 × 1.3 × 2.0 = 38.278 ✓
end note

Scorer -> Scorer: 1. Get TF for term in repo\n   (term frequency from postings)

Scorer -> Scorer: 2. Calculate IDF\n   log(totalDocs / documentFrequency)

Scorer -> Scorer: 3. Calculate base score\n   TF × IDF

Scorer -> Scorer: 4. Apply metadata boosts:\n   - Language (1.3× for major languages)\n   - Stars (1.2-2.0× based on count)\n   - Recency (optional future feature)\n   - PageRank (future feature)

Scorer -> Scorer: 5. Final score = base score × boosts

Scorer -> Results: Return ranked results\n(sorted by score descending)
deactivate Scorer

== RESULT FORMATTING ==
activate Results

Results -> Results: Extract repo metadata:\n- Owner/repo name\n- Star count\n- Language\n- Description

Results -> Results: Extract snippet from README:\n- Find first 100 chars\n- Clean markdown:\n  - Remove ![images](urls)\n  - Remove [links](urls)\n  - Remove **bold**\n  - Remove `code`\n  - Remove headers\n  - Remove tables

Results -> Results: Get term metadata:\n- Frequency in repo\n- Density percentage\n  (frequency / total terms)

Results -> Display: Return formatted results
deactivate Results

== DISPLAY ==
activate Display

Display -> User: Display results:\n\n1. encode/django-rest-framework\n   29974 ⭐ | Python | Score: 38.278\n   Web APIs for Django. 🎸...\n   freq: 5 | density: 0.87%\n\n2. aio-libs/aiohttp\n   16405 ⭐ | Python | Score: 7.656\n   Async HTTP framework...\n   freq: 0 | density: 0%

deactivate Display

note right of Scorer
  TF-IDF balances:
  - Frequent terms (TF)
  - Discriminative terms (IDF)
  
  Boosts account for:
  - Popular repos (stars)
  - Language relevance
end note

@enduml
